  "implementation": [
    "Two additive APIs explicitly read retained v1\u2013v6 archives and serialize canonical v6. Source-history and approval-lineage annotations accept v1 or v2 without new record fields.",
    "A separate closed v6 registry adds exactly eight source-v2 records. Shared codec primitives preserve legacy numbers, Decimal scales, datetime offsets, capture strings and omitted unknown coverage.",
    "Mixed source history validates contiguous corrections, exact heads, request and actor/key identity, same-year original/intermediate/effective observations and actual withdrawal references. Company-wide off-year Governance commitments do not imply local RF coverage.",
    "Retained lineage binds saved previews, versioned annual policy, complete approval manifests, review evidence, claims, predecessors, journals and feedback. V3 requires source-v2 and review-v3; legacy approvals retain their original versioned behavior.",
    "V6 owner-wire comparisons repair equality accepting different UTC-offset representations. Two independently reproduced pre-fix failures are preserved; later scale/lineage probes first ran after repair.",
    "Existing archive APIs, registries and validation order remain unchanged through exact private extraction. New serialization requires captured history, overrides and withdrawals, including explicit empty collections."
  ],
